{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QHookDimension","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.bar_distinguishes_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.bar_distinguishes_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QIntegerBarParity.lean#L127-L134","doc":"**The two forms are not interchangeable under bar.**  Concretely at `n = 2`:\nbalanced is fixed by `σ`, geometric is scaled by `q⁻¹`.  Recorded as the smallest\nwitness that the distinction is real rather than formal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.qIntPoly_bar_even_forces_degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.qIntPoly_bar_even_forces_degenerate","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QIntegerBarParity.lean#L108-L125","doc":"**The separating statement, in usable contrapositive form.**\n\nIf the geometric form were bar-even at `n` — i.e. `qIntPoly q⁻¹ n = qIntPoly q n`\n— then the covariance factor `q⁻¹^(n−1)` must act trivially on it.  Combined with\n`qIntPoly_bar_covariant`, bar-evenness of the geometric form forces\n\n    `(q⁻¹^(n−1) − 1) · qIntPoly q n = 0`,\n\nso it holds only in the degenerate cases: `n ≤ 1` (where the sum is `0` or `1`),\n`q^(n−1) = 1`, or `qIntPoly q n = 0`.  Away from those, the geometric form is\ngenuinely not bar-even, so it cannot carry a bar-even quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.qIntPoly_bar_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.qIntPoly_bar_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QIntegerBarParity.lean#L88-L106","doc":"**The geometric quantum integer is NOT bar-even — it is bar-COVARIANT**,\ntransforming with weight `−(n−1)`:\n\n`qIntPoly q⁻¹ n = q⁻¹^(n−1) · qIntPoly q n`.\n\nProof: `∑_{i<n} q^{−i}` is the same sum read backwards (`Finset.sum_range_reflect`),\nand backwards it is `∑_{i<n} q^{i−(n−1)}`, i.e. the forward sum scaled by\n`q^{−(n−1)}`.  Only `q ≠ 0` is needed — no `q ≠ 1`, and nothing archimedean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.qIntBal_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QIntegerBarParity.qIntBal_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QIntegerBarParity.lean#L69-L86","doc":"**The balanced quantum integer is BAR-EVEN.**\n\n`[n]_{q⁻¹} = [n]_q` — the bar involution `σ : q ↦ q⁻¹` fixes it.\n\nBoth the numerator and the denominator change sign under `σ`, and the two signs\ncancel.  This is the property that makes the balanced form the one compatible\nwith the corpus's bar-even / bar-odd channel decomposition.\n\nNo hypothesis at all: `inv_inv` holds unconditionally in a field, so this is an\nidentity of the *definition*, not a statement about a regular `q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}